1
00:00:19,315 --> 00:00:20,801
Hey, yo!

2
00:00:30,470 --> 00:00:31,550
I’ve got something for you.

3
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:38,756
Why is there so much money?

4
00:00:38,928 --> 00:00:40,143
I got a new job.

5
00:00:40,417 --> 00:00:43,257
It’s at a convenience store. Easy work, good pay.

6
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:44,730
You don’t have to worry anymore.

7
00:00:46,362 --> 00:00:48,242
You’ll finally have money to go back to school.

8
00:00:50,542 --> 00:00:51,982
Who said I was going back to school?

9
00:00:52,086 --> 00:00:54,399
I have to work too, so we can help each other.

10
00:00:56,193 --> 00:00:57,646
I don’t need your help.

11
00:00:58,011 --> 00:01:00,424
I can take care of my little sister.

12
00:01:02,192 --> 00:01:04,455
Besides, I won’t be some low-level employee forever.

13
00:01:04,702 --> 00:01:06,370
I’m going to rise all the way to

14
00:01:06,511 --> 00:01:07,527
store owner.

15
00:01:08,351 --> 00:01:09,750
Wow, look at you.

16
00:01:10,119 --> 00:01:11,119
Big talk!

17
00:01:12,950 --> 00:01:13,260
Huh?

18
00:01:13,315 --> 00:01:14,494
What? What?

19
00:01:14,756 --> 00:01:15,246
Come on.

20
00:01:15,293 --> 00:01:17,413
You don’t even know if you’ll survive as an employee.

21
00:01:18,266 --> 00:01:19,973
Come on, let’s practice.

22
00:01:21,351 --> 00:01:23,584
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

23
00:02:47,941 --> 00:02:50,270
Wow, where have you been?

24
00:02:50,547 --> 00:02:52,000
You’re back late.

25
00:02:52,658 --> 00:02:54,428
Look, it’s almost eight.

26
00:02:58,396 --> 00:03:00,613
Nava was hungry.

27
00:03:00,699 --> 00:03:02,343
There was nothing in the fridge,

28
00:03:02,783 --> 00:03:04,763
so I fried her some eggs.

29
00:03:06,323 --> 00:03:08,143
Thank you for looking after Nava.

30
00:03:12,637 --> 00:03:13,637
Come on.

31
00:03:13,746 --> 00:03:15,823
It’s nothing. It was no trouble.

32
00:03:16,359 --> 00:03:19,704
But next time you’re going to be late, give me a call.

33
00:03:19,852 --> 00:03:20,852
It’s all right.

34
00:03:21,453 --> 00:03:23,080
I probably won’t need to trouble you again.

35
00:03:23,104 --> 00:03:24,516
Why not?

36
00:03:25,084 --> 00:03:26,384
Is the job no good?

37
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,414
He chanted every day.

38
00:03:40,447 --> 00:03:41,880
But it was no use.

39
00:03:43,369 --> 00:03:45,883
I kept telling him to follow the rules.

40
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:50,403
Now I have to recruit a new night-shift employee again.

41
00:03:56,390 --> 00:03:57,430
What on earth is going on?

42
00:03:59,737 --> 00:04:00,765
Is Bird really dead?

43
00:04:05,023 --> 00:04:06,023
Cherd.

44
00:04:06,289 --> 00:04:08,526
I’ve already thrown Bird’s hand out behind the store.

45
00:04:09,007 --> 00:04:10,007
Okay.

46
00:04:10,596 --> 00:04:11,167
Here.

47
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:12,792
I’ll throw it away.

48
00:04:13,537 --> 00:04:14,575
Thank you so much, Dear.

49
00:04:15,951 --> 00:04:20,108
I think we should clean up these bloodstains.

50
00:04:21,255 --> 00:04:23,255
That should take us right to the end of the shift.

51
00:04:24,552 --> 00:04:25,552
Hey.

52
00:04:26,570 --> 00:04:28,157
Have you people lost your minds?

53
00:04:30,603 --> 00:04:31,686
A man died!

54
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,150
I’m calling the police.

55
00:04:39,283 --> 00:04:40,283
Wait.

56
00:04:43,203 --> 00:04:44,923
You said you were going to call the police.

57
00:04:45,556 --> 00:04:46,836
What are you going to tell them?

58
00:04:47,364 --> 00:04:49,596
“My coworker was killed by a ghost.

59
00:04:50,463 --> 00:04:52,050
A ghost ate him alive.

60
00:04:52,075 --> 00:04:53,355
All that was left was his hand.”

61
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:55,710
Do you think they’d believe you?

62
00:04:57,477 --> 00:04:58,477
Mr. Metha.

63
00:04:59,743 --> 00:05:01,357
You used to be a police officer, too.

64
00:05:02,563 --> 00:05:03,597
You know...

65
00:05:04,375 --> 00:05:07,155
If you tell them what really happened tonight,

66
00:05:08,095 --> 00:05:09,642
you know what will happen.

67
00:05:12,416 --> 00:05:13,416
I...

68
00:05:16,143 --> 00:05:17,143
You...

69
00:05:18,117 --> 00:05:19,117
Dear...

70
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:21,650
We will all become suspects.

71
00:05:23,219 --> 00:05:24,766
That’s right.

72
00:05:26,273 --> 00:05:27,539
You know it.

73
00:05:33,316 --> 00:05:35,123
Then what was the thing that ate Bird?

74
00:05:35,776 --> 00:05:37,023
A customer.

75
00:05:37,773 --> 00:05:38,973
I told you from the beginning.

76
00:05:40,159 --> 00:05:41,466
But don’t worry.

77
00:05:42,059 --> 00:05:43,183
Customers like that

78
00:05:43,498 --> 00:05:45,176
only show up after midnight.

79
00:05:45,856 --> 00:05:46,856
During the day,

80
00:05:46,921 --> 00:05:47,921
they’re harmless.

81
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:49,393
They never show themselves.

82
00:05:50,366 --> 00:05:51,505
So you mean...

83
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:53,605
we have to risk our lives like this every night?

84
00:05:55,190 --> 00:05:56,691
Now you can see

85
00:05:57,623 --> 00:05:59,356
why a convenience store job

86
00:06:00,096 --> 00:06:02,115
pays so much.

87
00:06:15,843 --> 00:06:16,843
Then I quit.

88
00:06:17,523 --> 00:06:18,523
Hey!

89
00:06:18,982 --> 00:06:19,775
You quit?

90
00:06:19,799 --> 00:06:21,548
I can’t take this every night.

91
00:06:21,915 --> 00:06:24,462
Think it over first. It’s just a job.

92
00:06:26,723 --> 00:06:27,723
Seriously.

93
00:06:28,348 --> 00:06:29,348
You...

94
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:31,816
You’re the most promising employee I’ve seen

95
00:06:32,136 --> 00:06:33,476
since I started working here.

96
00:06:38,503 --> 00:06:39,503
Here, Dear.

97
00:06:39,541 --> 00:06:40,292
10,000.

98
00:06:40,549 --> 00:06:41,549
Thank you.

99
00:06:45,096 --> 00:06:46,096
This money

100
00:06:46,743 --> 00:06:47,743
is for tonight.

101
00:06:49,198 --> 00:06:50,718
Count it and make sure it’s all there.

102
00:07:01,954 --> 00:07:04,471
Dear, get rid of that for me, then wipe up the blood.

103
00:07:04,496 --> 00:07:05,501
Okay, Cherd.

104
00:07:25,525 --> 00:07:26,525
Teacher!

105
00:07:30,570 --> 00:07:31,585
Study hard, Nava.

106
00:07:33,190 --> 00:07:34,630
I’ll pick you up this evening.

107
00:07:44,926 --> 00:07:45,926
Hello.

108
00:07:52,143 --> 00:07:53,450
Have you lost weight?

109
00:07:55,596 --> 00:07:56,805
I’m fine, Mom.

110
00:07:59,386 --> 00:08:00,959
How are Nam and Nava?

111
00:08:01,310 --> 00:08:02,310
Did they come with you?

112
00:08:03,479 --> 00:08:04,537
Nam...

113
00:08:06,332 --> 00:08:07,525
She is at work right now.

114
00:08:08,523 --> 00:08:11,413
Nava’s at school, so they couldn’t come.

115
00:08:15,943 --> 00:08:16,943
And...

116
00:08:17,483 --> 00:08:19,136
don’t you have to go to work?

117
00:08:19,536 --> 00:08:21,650
I’m on the night shift today, Mom.

118
00:08:24,776 --> 00:08:25,776
And when...

119
00:08:26,303 --> 00:08:28,516
will you finally get promoted to inspector?

120
00:08:31,862 --> 00:08:32,902
Probably not much longer.

121
00:08:34,097 --> 00:08:35,097
Because...

122
00:08:35,599 --> 00:08:37,210
I just closed a case recently.

123
00:08:40,586 --> 00:08:42,099
Good job, son.

124
00:08:44,493 --> 00:08:47,346
Next time you visit, wear your uniform, okay?

125
00:08:48,416 --> 00:08:49,416
I want to see it.

126
00:08:51,096 --> 00:08:52,096
Okay.

127
00:08:59,797 --> 00:09:00,797
Mom.

128
00:09:02,090 --> 00:09:03,543
Aren’t you hungry?

129
00:09:04,531 --> 00:09:06,785
The caregiver said you haven’t been eating anything.

130
00:09:08,248 --> 00:09:09,350
Please eat something.

131
00:09:16,809 --> 00:09:17,943
Mom.

132
00:09:19,848 --> 00:09:20,848
Mom.

133
00:09:24,607 --> 00:09:25,607
Mom.

134
00:09:28,529 --> 00:09:29,530
Mom!

135
00:09:32,660 --> 00:09:33,605
I’m sorry.

136
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:34,630
Mom.

137
00:09:35,461 --> 00:09:38,156
I was wrong. I was wrong.

138
00:09:39,643 --> 00:09:41,136
I was wrong.

139
00:09:41,501 --> 00:09:43,356
Could you please wait outside for a moment?

140
00:09:44,496 --> 00:09:45,628
Ms. Phen?

141
00:09:46,590 --> 00:09:47,590
Please step outside.

142
00:09:49,153 --> 00:09:50,153
Please calm down.

143
00:10:04,799 --> 00:10:06,356
(Job Application - Accountant Dear HR, Job Application-Sales Executive)

144
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:08,000
(Job Application - Human Resources (HR), Administrative Staff (Admin))

145
00:10:08,024 --> 00:10:09,803
(Dear HR Department, I would like
to submit my resume to apply for the Accountant position.)

146
00:10:09,827 --> 00:10:11,787
(I am highly interested in joining your company.)

147
00:10:50,825 --> 00:10:52,794
Hey! Open the door!

148
00:10:55,294 --> 00:10:56,294
Nava, come here.

149
00:10:58,463 --> 00:11:01,391
Hey! I said open the door!

150
00:11:07,572 --> 00:11:08,078
Hey!

151
00:11:08,103 --> 00:11:09,103
Nava.

152
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:11,147
Wait for me. Don’t come out.

153
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,275
I said open the door!

154
00:11:13,299 --> 00:11:14,299
Trust me, okay?

155
00:11:21,492 --> 00:11:23,039
Open the door, or I’ll break in!

156
00:11:23,343 --> 00:11:24,343
Metha!

157
00:11:39,055 --> 00:11:41,070
Here’s the 10,000 baht you asked for, sir.

158
00:11:46,959 --> 00:11:48,986
I came all the way to your house.

159
00:11:49,609 --> 00:11:51,055
Aren’t you going to invite me in?

160
00:11:52,143 --> 00:11:55,076
I’m hurt, you know.

161
00:12:05,207 --> 00:12:06,646
10,000 baht is nothing.

162
00:12:07,644 --> 00:12:08,964
How’s that supposed to be enough?

163
00:12:10,021 --> 00:12:13,104
You need to get me 100,000.

164
00:12:13,632 --> 00:12:14,677
100,000?

165
00:12:15,998 --> 00:12:17,256
I only borrowed a million.

166
00:12:18,387 --> 00:12:19,944
Only a million?

167
00:12:20,392 --> 00:12:23,896
Your debt’s up to three million now.

168
00:12:26,303 --> 00:12:27,303
Three million?

169
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:31,446
How did it get to three million?

170
00:12:31,955 --> 00:12:33,855
Ever heard of interest?

171
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:37,351
If you can’t pay,

172
00:12:38,352 --> 00:12:40,484
you’ll have to pay me another way.

173
00:12:50,467 --> 00:12:51,976
What about your daughter?

174
00:12:53,436 --> 00:12:57,223
Isn't she going to come out and greet your guests?

175
00:12:58,220 --> 00:12:59,916
How rude.

176
00:13:01,109 --> 00:13:02,309
Leave my daughter out of this.

177
00:13:02,394 --> 00:13:03,394
Get out of my way!

178
00:13:03,653 --> 00:13:04,653
Leave her alone.

179
00:13:05,747 --> 00:13:06,938
Let go of me!

180
00:13:08,085 --> 00:13:09,085
Nava!

181
00:13:12,027 --> 00:13:13,497
Open the door for me, sweetheart.

182
00:13:15,963 --> 00:13:16,963
Nava.

183
00:13:17,657 --> 00:13:18,836
Stay away from my daughter!

184
00:13:29,291 --> 00:13:32,406
What can a guy like you do?

185
00:13:33,115 --> 00:13:34,763
If you owe me, pay up.

186
00:13:36,377 --> 00:13:37,377
Nava!

187
00:13:37,870 --> 00:13:39,068
Open the door!

188
00:13:39,809 --> 00:13:41,303
Nava!

189
00:13:41,644 --> 00:13:42,673
Open the door!

190
00:13:43,942 --> 00:13:44,942
You stupid kid!

191
00:13:45,717 --> 00:13:47,563
Open the door, you stupid kid!

192
00:13:55,983 --> 00:13:57,077
Calm down.

193
00:13:59,391 --> 00:14:00,391
Calm down.

194
00:14:01,743 --> 00:14:02,743
Get out of my house.

195
00:14:07,377 --> 00:14:08,377
Go!

196
00:14:37,583 --> 00:14:38,583
Nava.

197
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:44,780
Can you stay with Auntie Jaem tonight?

198
00:15:23,954 --> 00:15:25,118
Can I help you?

199
00:15:31,853 --> 00:15:32,853
Well...

200
00:15:34,630 --> 00:15:37,255
Is it okay if I come back as a night-shift employee?

201
00:15:37,834 --> 00:15:38,834
Come on.

202
00:15:39,326 --> 00:15:41,529
We’re always happy to welcome back

203
00:15:42,029 --> 00:15:44,014
experienced employees.

204
00:15:44,586 --> 00:15:45,586
Of course you can.

205
00:15:49,749 --> 00:15:52,841
But could I get an advance for the next 10 days?

206
00:15:57,327 --> 00:15:58,327
10 days.

207
00:16:00,147 --> 00:16:01,444
Yes, well...

208
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:05,233
I need a lot of money for something urgent.

209
00:16:08,367 --> 00:16:11,068
I promise I’ll come to work every day.

210
00:16:11,556 --> 00:16:12,676
I won’t miss a single shift.

211
00:16:15,204 --> 00:16:19,130
And how can you be sure you’ll last the full ten days?

212
00:16:30,229 --> 00:16:31,783
I’ll do whatever it takes to survive.

213
00:16:35,107 --> 00:16:36,287
Actually,

214
00:16:38,341 --> 00:16:40,341
I don’t have the authority to approve this myself.

215
00:17:04,053 --> 00:17:05,053
All right.

216
00:17:05,506 --> 00:17:06,506
Ten days.

217
00:17:07,349 --> 00:17:09,404
I’ll approve the 10-day advance.

218
00:17:11,748 --> 00:17:12,748
Really?

219
00:17:12,873 --> 00:17:13,873
Yes.

220
00:17:14,115 --> 00:17:15,155
Thank you so much.

221
00:17:16,275 --> 00:17:19,080
Then work hard,

222
00:17:19,650 --> 00:17:22,744
and don’t forget to follow every rule.

223
00:17:32,361 --> 00:17:33,361
I will.

224
00:17:58,017 --> 00:18:00,399
When did you start working here?

225
00:18:03,188 --> 00:18:05,182
Just yesterday.

226
00:18:05,424 --> 00:18:06,424
Night shift?

227
00:18:07,030 --> 00:18:08,030
Yeah.

228
00:18:08,611 --> 00:18:10,284
I want to work the night shift, too.

229
00:18:10,682 --> 00:18:12,976
Cherd says it’s always fully staffed.

230
00:18:14,358 --> 00:18:15,217
Fully staffed?

231
00:18:15,339 --> 00:18:16,339
Yes.

232
00:18:19,355 --> 00:18:21,078
Dear.

233
00:18:22,076 --> 00:18:23,937
I’m going home.

234
00:18:24,174 --> 00:18:25,463
Then go. Who’s stopping you?

235
00:18:25,995 --> 00:18:27,554
Aren’t you going to ask me to stay?

236
00:18:27,633 --> 00:18:28,225
Nope.

237
00:18:28,519 --> 00:18:29,655
You’re so mean.

238
00:18:33,350 --> 00:18:35,542
Isn’t Bird coming to work?

239
00:18:39,476 --> 00:18:40,828
He won’t be coming back.

240
00:18:41,985 --> 00:18:43,040
He’s gone for good.

241
00:18:48,143 --> 00:18:49,303
He went back to his hometown?

242
00:18:50,019 --> 00:18:51,019
That was sudden.

243
00:18:54,331 --> 00:18:55,331
Then...

244
00:18:55,690 --> 00:18:57,169
There must be an opening on the night shift now!

245
00:18:57,193 --> 00:18:58,574
Then I'll work the night shift.

246
00:18:58,722 --> 00:18:59,722
Absolutely not.

247
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:01,724
Why not?

248
00:19:02,235 --> 00:19:03,254
You’re annoying.

249
00:19:04,131 --> 00:19:05,131
Look.

250
00:19:05,279 --> 00:19:07,467
Dear is always picking on me.

251
00:19:09,739 --> 00:19:11,019
Because you really are annoying.

252
00:19:11,342 --> 00:19:12,992
Finish your work and go home.

253
00:19:13,049 --> 00:19:14,209
You’re always kicking me out.

254
00:19:14,428 --> 00:19:16,129
It’s late.

255
00:19:17,414 --> 00:19:18,414
Are you worried about me?

256
00:19:18,705 --> 00:19:20,870
Enough. Go home.

257
00:19:26,871 --> 00:19:27,871
Bye.

258
00:19:40,393 --> 00:19:44,313
Does what happened to Bird happen often?

259
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:50,772
If they don’t die,

260
00:19:51,850 --> 00:19:52,850
they disappear.

261
00:19:54,654 --> 00:19:56,254
Some never come back to work.

262
00:20:00,881 --> 00:20:01,881
What about you?

263
00:20:02,161 --> 00:20:04,519
You quit. Why come back?

264
00:20:13,328 --> 00:20:14,448
Or is it just for the money?

265
00:20:18,601 --> 00:20:19,601
It’s obvious.

266
00:20:22,586 --> 00:20:23,986
Don’t you care about your own life?

267
00:20:24,372 --> 00:20:26,169
And you didn’t take this job for the money?

268
00:20:27,594 --> 00:20:29,074
Don’t assume everyone’s like you.

269
00:20:37,063 --> 00:20:38,352
Go on, get out.

270
00:20:39,266 --> 00:20:40,906
Or do you want to watch me get undressed?

271
00:20:54,375 --> 00:20:56,453
Inspect deliveries from the delivery truck

272
00:20:56,478 --> 00:20:57,478
at the designated time.

273
00:20:57,734 --> 00:20:58,734
Rule number 12.

274
00:20:59,132 --> 00:21:01,372
Please observe the lights inside this convenience store.

275
00:21:01,997 --> 00:21:02,997
Please observe the lights

276
00:21:03,348 --> 00:21:05,413
inside the convenience store while on duty.

277
00:21:05,579 --> 00:21:09,272
The lights inside the convenience store while on duty.

278
00:21:10,153 --> 00:21:11,887
In an emergency,

279
00:21:12,449 --> 00:21:15,146
employees may only use the tools provided by the store.

280
00:21:17,134 --> 00:21:18,414
The tools provided by the store.

281
00:21:18,664 --> 00:21:19,664
Dang it!

282
00:21:20,311 --> 00:21:21,311
Can you shut up?

283
00:21:22,279 --> 00:21:23,279
You’re annoying.

284
00:21:24,279 --> 00:21:25,279
Sorry.

285
00:21:25,751 --> 00:21:27,071
I’m afraid I’ll forget the rules.

286
00:21:29,497 --> 00:21:31,457
Memorizing the rules doesn’t mean you’ll survive.

287
00:21:32,387 --> 00:21:34,015
Those things are crafty.

288
00:21:40,099 --> 00:21:42,046
So what exactly are those things?

289
00:21:54,090 --> 00:21:56,602
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

290
00:22:13,868 --> 00:22:15,527
Would you like a minced pork bun?

291
00:22:15,655 --> 00:22:17,303
We have a buy-one-get-one-free promotion.

292
00:22:30,727 --> 00:22:32,698
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

293
00:22:32,723 --> 00:22:33,964
Please come again.

294
00:22:40,279 --> 00:22:42,539
Was that customer... human?

295
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:44,280
Yeah.

296
00:22:46,762 --> 00:22:49,756
Then how are we supposed to tell who’s normal?

297
00:22:51,986 --> 00:22:53,554
You’ll know when the time comes.

298
00:22:56,080 --> 00:22:57,324
If you know anything, tell me.

299
00:22:58,207 --> 00:22:59,246
We have to work together.

300
00:23:02,309 --> 00:23:03,309
At least...

301
00:23:05,396 --> 00:23:07,316
you could show me how to use this cash register.

302
00:23:19,545 --> 00:23:20,978
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

303
00:23:22,458 --> 00:23:23,505
Are you new here?

304
00:23:27,558 --> 00:23:28,558
Yes, I am.

305
00:23:29,185 --> 00:23:31,015
I'm here to buy toothpaste,

306
00:23:32,866 --> 00:23:34,538
but I don’t know where it is.

307
00:23:36,083 --> 00:23:37,083
Young man.

308
00:23:38,458 --> 00:23:39,780
Could you help me?

309
00:23:42,685 --> 00:23:43,803
The toothpaste is this way.

310
00:23:44,411 --> 00:23:45,694
Please follow me.

311
00:24:03,481 --> 00:24:04,674
That’ll be 58 baht.

312
00:24:04,791 --> 00:24:05,875
We have a special offer.

313
00:24:05,909 --> 00:24:08,545
Pair it with a toothpaste for just 60 baht

314
00:24:08,570 --> 00:24:09,970
instead of the regular price of 75.

315
00:24:10,064 --> 00:24:11,064
Would you like to get it?

316
00:24:12,610 --> 00:24:13,790
No, thank you.

317
00:24:47,351 --> 00:24:48,524
Five...

318
00:24:49,278 --> 00:24:50,278
Six...

319
00:24:50,658 --> 00:24:51,658
Fifty-seven.

320
00:24:54,485 --> 00:24:55,680
You’re one baht short.

321
00:24:56,984 --> 00:24:58,752
Count it again, dear.

322
00:25:27,023 --> 00:25:28,110
Fifty-seven.

323
00:25:28,135 --> 00:25:29,535
You’re still one baht short, ma'am.

324
00:26:04,378 --> 00:26:06,031
Count it again, dear.

325
00:26:20,203 --> 00:26:21,234
That’s the full amount.

326
00:26:28,905 --> 00:26:30,293
No bag, thank you.

327
00:26:31,351 --> 00:26:32,758
Save the planet.

328
00:26:47,378 --> 00:26:48,873
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

329
00:27:02,572 --> 00:27:03,572
Oh.

330
00:27:03,978 --> 00:27:05,658
You know how to use the cash register now.

331
00:27:05,758 --> 00:27:07,571
You can work the counter from now on.

332
00:27:09,332 --> 00:27:11,045
Just remember to follow the rules.

333
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:02,219
Rule number four.

334
00:28:02,307 --> 00:28:03,904
Employees must greet customers, thank them,

335
00:28:03,928 --> 00:28:05,991
and inform them of promotions.

336
00:28:17,378 --> 00:28:19,260
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

337
00:28:29,965 --> 00:28:31,562
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

338
00:28:31,908 --> 00:28:32,908
Please come again.

339
00:28:36,087 --> 00:28:37,567
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

340
00:28:38,380 --> 00:28:39,380
Please come again.

341
00:28:51,625 --> 00:28:52,825
Why don’t you use the glasses?

342
00:28:55,585 --> 00:28:56,585
What glasses?

343
00:28:56,618 --> 00:28:58,016
The store equipment

344
00:28:59,199 --> 00:29:00,751
we use in emergencies.

345
00:29:01,826 --> 00:29:02,826
These glasses...

346
00:29:03,043 --> 00:29:04,697
let night-shift employees like us

347
00:29:05,222 --> 00:29:06,997
see the special customers.

348
00:29:08,599 --> 00:29:09,599
You didn’t know?

349
00:29:09,668 --> 00:29:10,668
I had no idea.

350
00:29:16,685 --> 00:29:17,685
What's the matter?

351
00:29:24,391 --> 00:29:26,031
Why didn’t you tell me about the glasses?

352
00:29:26,811 --> 00:29:28,051
I almost broke a rule just now.

353
00:29:29,250 --> 00:29:30,317
You didn’t ask.

354
00:29:31,011 --> 00:29:32,550
Besides, I was busy.

355
00:29:33,121 --> 00:29:34,448
I was following the rules, too.

356
00:29:34,667 --> 00:29:36,200
Do I really have to ask about something that important?

357
00:29:36,224 --> 00:29:38,001
You know how dangerous this place is.

358
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:39,026
So what?

359
00:29:39,640 --> 00:29:41,460
Do I have to follow you around every second?

360
00:29:42,688 --> 00:29:43,890
This isn’t a small matter.

361
00:29:44,694 --> 00:29:45,814
People’s lives are at stake.

362
00:29:48,354 --> 00:29:50,674
Have you gotten so used to it that you don’t care anymore?

363
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:52,748
Yeah.

364
00:29:52,812 --> 00:29:53,812
That’s just how I am.

365
00:29:54,294 --> 00:29:55,810
I don't care about anyone.

366
00:29:55,974 --> 00:29:57,681
I'm selfish. So what?

367
00:29:57,706 --> 00:29:59,434
Shouldn’t you at least have some humanity?

368
00:29:59,459 --> 00:30:00,904
You’re the one who keeps thinking

369
00:30:01,177 --> 00:30:02,461
someone else will come save you.

370
00:30:03,108 --> 00:30:04,634
If you can’t survive on your own,

371
00:30:05,441 --> 00:30:06,641
even if I told you everything,

372
00:30:06,836 --> 00:30:08,616
you still wouldn’t make it.

373
00:30:14,645 --> 00:30:15,738
I’m going to take a break.

374
00:30:25,791 --> 00:30:26,791
Dear.

375
00:30:28,144 --> 00:30:29,241
You know very well

376
00:30:30,036 --> 00:30:32,863
that no one can work the night shift at Sunny Mart alone.

377
00:30:33,756 --> 00:30:35,668
If you let something like this happen again,

378
00:30:37,416 --> 00:30:38,889
you’ll be the one in trouble.

379
00:30:44,531 --> 00:30:45,531
Who knows?

380
00:30:46,938 --> 00:30:47,938
Maybe Metha

381
00:30:48,411 --> 00:30:50,546
could help solve your problem one day.

382
00:30:52,254 --> 00:30:53,254
You never know.

383
00:30:58,209 --> 00:31:00,324
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

384
00:32:27,245 --> 00:32:28,245
Whoa!

385
00:33:11,611 --> 00:33:12,611
Hey, bro.

386
00:33:13,685 --> 00:33:14,685
Hey.

387
00:33:22,251 --> 00:33:23,851
How long have you been doing this, Good?

388
00:33:27,037 --> 00:33:28,239
Oh...

389
00:33:28,849 --> 00:33:30,145
So long I’ve lost track, bro.

390
00:33:31,139 --> 00:33:32,139
What’s up?

391
00:33:32,478 --> 00:33:34,271
Good, do you know what this store really is?

392
00:33:39,931 --> 00:33:41,007
I’m not really sure.

393
00:33:43,559 --> 00:33:45,658
I just know the pay’s good, so people give it a try.

394
00:33:46,798 --> 00:33:47,798
But...

395
00:33:47,869 --> 00:33:49,133
they never last long.

396
00:33:56,031 --> 00:33:57,569
Has anyone stayed for a long time?

397
00:33:58,178 --> 00:33:59,220
People don’t stick around.

398
00:34:00,713 --> 00:34:01,713
If you don’t count Cherd,

399
00:34:01,936 --> 00:34:03,643
the one who’s been here the longest is

400
00:34:04,010 --> 00:34:05,010
Dear.

401
00:34:05,637 --> 00:34:06,797
It’s been about three months.

402
00:34:08,363 --> 00:34:09,363
Three months?

403
00:34:09,730 --> 00:34:10,730
Yeah.

404
00:34:11,236 --> 00:34:12,534
Most people come and go.

405
00:34:13,410 --> 00:34:14,410
They...

406
00:34:14,441 --> 00:34:16,504
they say they can’t handle the customers.

407
00:34:21,723 --> 00:34:22,723
Good.

408
00:34:24,556 --> 00:34:26,161
What exactly are these customers?

409
00:34:26,916 --> 00:34:27,916
Ghosts?

410
00:34:28,341 --> 00:34:29,341
Spirits?

411
00:34:41,198 --> 00:34:42,563
It doesn't matter what they are.

412
00:34:45,358 --> 00:34:46,358
One thing’s for sure.

413
00:34:47,005 --> 00:34:48,147
They can kill you.

414
00:34:52,358 --> 00:34:53,731
They’re just waiting for a chance.

415
00:34:54,811 --> 00:34:56,132
Waiting for you to make a mistake.

416
00:34:56,156 --> 00:34:57,156
Just once.

417
00:35:03,011 --> 00:35:05,553
If you see anything strange, just follow the rules.

418
00:35:10,251 --> 00:35:11,785
Oh, and...

419
00:35:14,081 --> 00:35:16,681
Don’t trust anything that looks too much like a person.

420
00:35:39,403 --> 00:35:40,403
Here. Take the glasses.

421
00:35:42,631 --> 00:35:43,254
No, thanks.

422
00:35:43,583 --> 00:35:45,023
I thought you said it was essential.

423
00:35:50,044 --> 00:35:51,913
Don’t I have to survive on my own?

424
00:35:55,991 --> 00:35:56,991
Suit yourself.

425
00:35:57,771 --> 00:35:59,031
Just don’t blame me later.

426
00:36:02,804 --> 00:36:04,874
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

427
00:36:10,764 --> 00:36:11,667
Rule number 12.

428
00:36:11,692 --> 00:36:13,514
When the lights turn green,

429
00:36:13,584 --> 00:36:14,862
employees must never make eye contact

430
00:36:14,886 --> 00:36:16,654
with customers who enter the store.

431
00:36:24,478 --> 00:36:27,111
I want betel nut... and betel leaves...

432
00:36:29,739 --> 00:36:31,958
I want betel nut and betel leaves.

433
00:36:38,021 --> 00:36:40,463
I want betel nut and betel leaves.

434
00:36:45,261 --> 00:36:46,261
Just a moment, sir.

435
00:36:53,891 --> 00:36:55,691
The betel nut and leaves are in this section.

436
00:36:56,010 --> 00:36:57,284
Please follow me.

437
00:37:05,099 --> 00:37:06,099
Dear.

438
00:37:08,371 --> 00:37:09,371
Dear, help me!

439
00:37:13,576 --> 00:37:14,576
Dear!

440
00:37:19,838 --> 00:37:20,838
Help me!

441
00:37:39,851 --> 00:37:40,851
This way, sir.

442
00:38:09,044 --> 00:38:10,044
Where is it?

443
00:38:11,638 --> 00:38:12,638
Where is it?

444
00:38:14,571 --> 00:38:15,728
Please wait a moment, sir.

445
00:39:15,657 --> 00:39:16,657
Dear!

446
00:39:20,671 --> 00:39:21,671
Dear!

447
00:39:24,812 --> 00:39:25,812
Dear, are you here?

448
00:40:09,164 --> 00:40:10,164
Dear!

449
00:40:11,364 --> 00:40:12,364
Keep quiet.

450
00:40:15,056 --> 00:40:16,056
But...

451
00:40:19,091 --> 00:40:21,184
I knew I’d find you here sooner or later.

452
00:40:21,851 --> 00:40:22,891
We’re getting out of here.

453
00:40:23,791 --> 00:40:25,106
Come on. Let’s go.

454
00:40:25,851 --> 00:40:26,851
There you are.

455
00:40:28,801 --> 00:40:29,801
Who’s that?

456
00:40:33,589 --> 00:40:34,589
This is my brother.

457
00:40:35,309 --> 00:40:36,942
I won’t let them take him.

458
00:40:39,123 --> 00:40:40,123
No.

459
00:40:40,443 --> 00:40:41,763
You have to return him to them right now.

460
00:40:41,787 --> 00:40:43,650
No! What would you know?

461
00:40:44,534 --> 00:40:45,534
Come on, Den.

462
00:40:47,254 --> 00:40:48,587
What’s your problem?

463
00:40:50,114 --> 00:40:51,158
I'm taking Den away.

464
00:40:51,183 --> 00:40:52,183
Dear.

465
00:40:54,453 --> 00:40:55,614
That's not your brother.

466
00:41:35,219 --> 00:41:36,219
Dear!

467
00:41:40,008 --> 00:41:41,008
Dear.

468
00:42:04,851 --> 00:42:06,818
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

469
00:42:17,707 --> 00:42:19,476
Every time the lights turn green,

470
00:42:20,194 --> 00:42:22,740
this customer comes into the store carrying a sack.

471
00:42:23,101 --> 00:42:24,154
And inside that sack,

472
00:42:24,721 --> 00:42:26,010
it takes the form of someone

473
00:42:26,478 --> 00:42:27,478
we’re thinking about,

474
00:42:27,718 --> 00:42:28,718
to lure its victims.

475
00:42:31,338 --> 00:42:32,338
Just now,

476
00:42:33,045 --> 00:42:34,525
If Metha hadn’t helped,

477
00:42:34,787 --> 00:42:36,497
Dear would’ve been caught in the sack

478
00:42:36,867 --> 00:42:38,388
and become its replacement victim.

479
00:42:41,994 --> 00:42:42,994
These things...

480
00:42:43,380 --> 00:42:45,180
They’re not just coming in to shop, are they?

481
00:42:45,674 --> 00:42:48,090
They seem to be deliberately choosing people.

482
00:42:48,747 --> 00:42:50,227
Each one has its own way of doing it.

483
00:42:50,920 --> 00:42:51,920
That’s right.

484
00:42:52,941 --> 00:42:53,941
That’s why

485
00:42:54,339 --> 00:42:56,285
our employees have to look out for one another,

486
00:42:57,996 --> 00:42:59,082
so no one

487
00:43:00,464 --> 00:43:01,464
breaks the rules.

488
00:43:05,798 --> 00:43:06,798
But for now...

489
00:43:11,468 --> 00:43:13,492
we’d better clean up this store.

490
00:43:15,865 --> 00:43:16,898
It’s a complete mess.

491
00:43:18,159 --> 00:43:19,159
The morning shift staff

492
00:43:21,751 --> 00:43:22,981
will be shocked.

493
00:43:39,384 --> 00:43:40,584
About what happened earlier...

494
00:43:43,718 --> 00:43:44,718
Thanks.

495
00:43:46,011 --> 00:43:47,011
It’s nothing.

496
00:43:53,198 --> 00:43:54,198
What’s that?

497
00:43:55,371 --> 00:43:56,791
Do you have Instagram?

498
00:44:00,370 --> 00:44:02,476
If not, your phone number will do.

499
00:44:29,971 --> 00:44:30,971
I’m heading out.

500
00:44:34,958 --> 00:44:35,958
Yeah.

501
00:45:01,338 --> 00:45:06,324
(Help me!)

502
00:45:11,906 --> 00:45:12,539
What's this?

503
00:45:12,702 --> 00:45:13,398
I got it for you.

504
00:45:13,593 --> 00:45:14,953
Have you always lived alone, Dear?

505
00:45:15,080 --> 00:45:16,429
That must get lonely.

506
00:45:17,091 --> 00:45:18,091
Don’t worry.

507
00:45:18,156 --> 00:45:19,312
I don’t think anything will happen tonight.

508
00:45:19,336 --> 00:45:20,576
It’s the quiet nights like this

509
00:45:22,176 --> 00:45:23,176
that are scarier.

510
00:45:28,724 --> 00:45:29,724
You two!

511
00:45:30,016 --> 00:45:31,282
Get away from the counter!

512
00:45:31,469 --> 00:45:32,469
Store rule.

513
00:45:33,171 --> 00:45:33,989
The counter must not be left unattended

514
00:45:34,013 --> 00:45:35,039
for more than three minutes.

515
00:45:35,063 --> 00:45:36,641
I don’t care about your stupid rules!

516
00:45:36,750 --> 00:45:38,367
Is this really all there is?
